.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-tokens - List supported tokens (symbols used in --token)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 tokens [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the token catalog.

.PP
Includes RETIRED tokens by default (an existing payment references its token
forever, so they stay listed and resolvable); each row carries an "active" flag.
Only an active token can be used for a NEW payment — pass --active to list just
those, or --active=false to see only the retired ones.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--active\fP[=false]
	Filter by active flag (--active, or --active=false for retired only); omit for every token

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--chain-id\fP=0
	Filter by EVM chain ID (e.g. 5042002)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tokens

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--symbol\fP=""
	Filter by token symbol (case-insensitive, e.g. USDC)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 tokens
  rail0 tokens --chain-id 5042002
  rail0 tokens --symbol USDC
  rail0 tokens --active           # only what a new payment can use
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP
